<title>USA: BankAmerica vice chairman Rossi to retire.</title>
<headline>BankAmerica vice chairman Rossi to retire.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>BankAmerica Corp said on Wednesday that Michael Rossi, vice chairman of BankAmerica and a member of the bank's Managing Committee, plans to retire from the company in the second quarter of the year.</p>
<p>Rossi, 52, said that he intends to &quot;retire from the banking profession&quot; and focus on projects he has long considered.  </p>
<p>BankAmerica did not name a replacement for Rossi.</p>
</text>
